: " \u2014", "lp": -0.7389274835586548, "top": [[" \u2014", -0.7389274835586548], [" =", -0.8445755243301392]]}, {"t": " Intel", "lp": -0.01615237258374691, "top": [[" Intel", -0.01615237258374691], [" C", -4.94443416595459]]}, {"t": " one", "lp": -0.10417279601097107, "top": [[" one", -0.10417279601097107], [" C", -2.756842851638794]]}, {"t": "API", "lp": -0.00995598640292883, "top": [["API", -0.00995598640292883], ["D", -4.696633815765381]]}, {"t": " D", "lp": -0.11714185029268265, "top": [[" D", -0.11714185029268265], [" C", -2.2175238132476807]]}, {"t": "PC", "lp": -0.0007272622315213084, "top": [["PC", -0.0007272622315213084], ["pc", -7.413498401641846]]}, {"t": "++", "lp": -0.0003144043148495257, "top": [["++", -0.0003144043148495257], ["+/", -8.212446212768555]]}], "text": "# PKGBUILD build() Function: Step-by-Step Explanation\n\nLet me break down this `build()` function line by line, explaining each flag and its purpose.\n\n## The Setup\n\n```bash\nsource /opt/intel/oneapi/setvars.sh --force\n```\nThis loads the Intel oneAPI environment variables (compiler paths, library paths, etc.). The `--force` flag forces the environment to be set up even if it was already sourced. Without this, `icx`/`icpx` wouldn't be found.\n\n```bash\nset -e\n```\nThis makes the script exit immediately if any command returns a non-zero status (an error). This is standard practice in build functions.\n\n## The CMake Invocation\n\n```bash\ncmake -S \"${srcdir}/llama.cpp\" -B \"${srcdir}/build\" -G Ninja\n```\n- `-S \"${srcdir}/llama.cpp\"` \u2014 **Source directory**: where the source code lives\n- `-B \"${srcdir}/build\"` \u2014 **Build directory**: where build artifacts go\n- `-G Ninja` \u2014 **Generator**: use Ninja (a fast build system) instead of Make\n\n## CMake Configuration Flags\n\n```bash\n-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release\n```\nOptimized build with compiler optimizations enabled (`-O3`), no debug symbols.\n\n```bash\n-DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr -DCMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR=lib\n```\n- Install prefix: `/usr` (standard system location)\n- Install lib dir: `lib` (ensures libraries go to `/usr/lib`, not `/usr/lib64`)\n\n```bash\n-DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=icx -DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=icpx\n```\nUse Intel's compilers:\n- `icx` \u2014 Intel oneAPI DPC++"}